-- REFUSAL FIXTURE, BLAWX-EXPORT-SPEC §11 W1 (integrated 2026-09-02).
--
-- W1's own note said the `RSOpaque` escape was "not known to be reachable in
-- the M1 fragment, and none was constructed". It is reachable, and this is the
-- construction: a record `DECLARE`d in an IMPORTed module reaches the Blawx
-- emitter as `RSOpaque "Shared Ontology.Player"` — a printed name with no
-- `RName` behind it — so `recordInSort` has nothing to look up in
-- `envDeclRecords` and the EQUALS below lowered at exit 0, emitting exactly
-- the `A = B` identity comparison the W1 refusal exists to stop.
--
-- `l4 check` succeeds on this module. The refusal is the Blawx leg's.

IMPORT `shared-ontology`

§ `Section`

@export Two players are the same player if they are equal.
GIVEN a IS A Player
      b IS A Player
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `same player` a b IF a EQUALS b
